.Dd May 27, 2026
.Dt BUILD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm build
.Nd create, compile, run, and bundle solutions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm make
.Cm new
.Ar spec ...
.Ar contest
.Nm make
.Cm run
.Ar index
.Ar contest
.Nm make
.Cm rerun
.Ar index
.Ar contest
.Nm make
.Cm check
.Ar index
.Ar contest
.Nm make
.Cm bundle
.Ar index
.Ar contest
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The build commands keep the submitted program and the tested program close
together.
The source is written once.
It is bundled before compilation and before submission.
.Pp
.Cm new
creates source files and test directories.
The last argument is the contest id.
Earlier arguments are problem indexes or ranges.
.Pp
.Cm run
bundles and compiles the source, then runs all
.Pa case-*.in
files in the matching test directory.
If a file with the same stem and suffix
.Pa .out
exists, output is compared against it.
Otherwise the output is printed.
.Pp
.Cm rerun
runs the cached binary in
.Pa .build/ .
It is useful after only a test has changed.
If the source is newer than the binary, it says so.
.Pp
.Cm check
is
.Cm run
with
.Ev CHECK=1 .
It asks the compiler for a stricter build, debug library checks, and
sanitizers when supported.
.Pp
.Cm bundle
prints the single file which should be submitted.
It recursively expands quoted includes found beside the source, in
.Pa include/ ,
or from the repository root.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa .build/A.71/main"
.It Pa solutions/A.71.cpp
Source for problem A in contest 71.
.It Pa tests/A.71/
Saved sample and local tests.
.It Pa .build/A.71/main
Compiled binary made by
.Cm run .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make new A 71
make new A-H 1985
make run A 71
make rerun all
make check A 71
make bundle A 71 > .build/A.71/submit.cpp
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr data 1 ,
.Xr test 1 ,
.Xr probs 7
